    {
     "kind": "test-defect",
     "sev": "low",
     "text": "Doc says the suite 'asserts that the filtered pipeline never reports a larger RMSSD than the raw one', and the test comment justifies it as 'removing outliers can only shrink a root-mean-square of differences'. That is false in general: the gated estimator drops pairs, and the RMS of a subset of differences can exceed the RMS of all of them. The assertion holds only empirically on these 20 fixtures, so a future fixture could fail it without any app defect.",
